  "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=6,$ we substitute $x=6$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-20{x}^{2} & =180 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-20(6)^{2} & =180 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-720 & =180 \\\\ {y}^{2}-80 & =20 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =80+20 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =100 \\\\ y & =\\pm 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $x=6$  at the points $(6,\\pm 10).$",
